  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for phase two of the Action for Voice, Influence, and Inclusive Development (AVID) project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The STAR-Ghana Foundation is a Ghanaian grantmaking organization that has supported more than 230 civil society organizations since it was founded in 2010. Its vision is a well-informed and active Ghanaian citizenry able to contribute to transformational change that advances democracy, accountability, and social inclusion. Its mission is to increase the effectiveness of citizens and civil society to achieve an equitable, inclusive society. This grant will support the second phase of the AVID program to strengthen the effectiveness of citizens&#x2019; actions for voice and equitable and inclusive access to benefits and relevant services. (Strategy: Inclusive Governance)</narrative>
  </description>
